            <ArticleTitle>Nifedipine-induced hypokalemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>370-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nifedipine, a calcium-channel blocking agent, has been reported to cause many side effects, particularly in the cardiovascular system. A case of nifedipine-induced hypokalemia is presented, with a discussion on the presumable mechanism involved in this phenomenon.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
